## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to reason about idempotency and delivery guarantees in CNPA patterns, at a beginner level, while nudging toward practical implementation details.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotent enrichment
- Exactly-once delivery
- Outbox pattern
- Deduplication cache
- Producer config (idempotence, acks)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: dedup check before processing
async function enrich(event, db, cache) {
  const id = event.event_id;
  if (await cache.has(id)) return; // already processed
  const profile = await db.getProfile(event.user_id);
  const enriched = { ...event, profile };
  await cache.add(id, /* ttl */ 60000);
  await publishToKafka(enriched);
  await writeOutbox(enriched);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test edge cases like cache eviction and outbox failures?
- How would you adapt if events arrive out of order or with duplicate IDs?

